# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "Raw markup carries no verdict"

# Nothing inside raw markup answers to wikitext, so the stray-bracket rule stops at the
# boundary of a fence, an inline tick and a typed block. A bracket in prose still reads as one.

Inline `a < b` code.
#          ^ - invalid.illegal.bad-angle-bracket.html.tiddlywiki5

```
a < b in a bare fence
# ^ - invalid.illegal.bad-angle-bracket.html.tiddlywiki5
```

```notalanguage
x < y
# ^ - invalid.illegal.bad-angle-bracket.html.tiddlywiki5
```

$$$text/plain
x < y
# ^ - invalid.illegal.bad-angle-bracket.html.tiddlywiki5
$$$

# A stray bracket in prose keeps its verdict.
A stray < in prose.
#       ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 invalid.illegal.bad-angle-bracket.html.tiddlywiki5

# An xml fence names its own grammar.
```xml
<a/>
```
